// A held value is read as any variable is: its type is the slot's, known
// where the hold binds it. A return synthesises the pure returner of what its
// value synthesises, the mode-correct reading of an introduction whose premise
// synthesises (Dunfield and Krishnaswami, "Bidirectional Typing", ACM
// Computing Surveys 54(5), 2021, doi:10.1145/3450952).

/// A held value returned to a statement that binds it: the binder states no
/// type, and the read synthesises the slot's (#1142).
@[ runs("3") ]
def bound() -> -F Integer {
  hold i = 3;
  run k <- pure i;
  pure k
}
